WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:15.687
"We can't open the wormhole again without magic!"

2
00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:16.667
Gliss exclaimed.

3
00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:19.829
"We could be trapped here forever!"

4
00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:24.071
Crash! Zann spun around as something landed behind them.

5
00:00:24.852 --> 00:00:27.413
It was a large platter of puckerberry pancakes!

6
00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:28.874
"The food!"

7
00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:29.594
Darb said.

8
00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:30.675
"It's here.

9
00:00:30.955 --> 00:00:32.676
I guess the spell worked after all."

10
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.562
"It just took a long time."

11
00:00:36.543 --> 00:00:39.265
Perda stuck her finger in the pancake syrup and licked it.

12
00:00:39.285 --> 00:00:45.790
"Mmm!" "It's weird that the spell took so long to work," Zann said.

13
00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.834
"We should try another spell and see if the same thing happens."

14
00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:51.355
"I'll do it."

15
00:00:51.615 --> 00:00:52.936
Perda rubbed her hands together.

16
00:00:52.956 --> 00:00:55.959
"Levitate!" They all waited.

17
00:00:56.279 --> 00:01:00.142
Several moments passed before Perda's feet finally lifted off the ground.

18
00:01:03.176 --> 00:01:06.497
"Magic must work really slowly here, that's all."

19
00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:09.279
Zann stepped toward the wormhole and waited.

20
00:01:10.219 --> 00:01:11.980
Eventually it swirled open again.

21
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.301
"Phew! We're not trapped after all."

22
00:01:15.321 --> 00:01:18.322
"Good." Perda reached for a pancake.

23
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:21.564
"Let's eat, and then we can look for Wyssa."

24
00:01:22.464 --> 00:01:23.965
Darb peered into the distance.

25
00:01:24.405 --> 00:01:25.245
"Someone's coming."

26
00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.587
Several people were moving slowly toward them.

27
00:01:29.487 --> 00:01:33.685
They were very slim and tall, with extra-long arms and legs.

28
00:01:34.686 --> 00:01:39.388
Their skin, hair, and clothes were the same dull colors as the rest of their world.

29
00:01:39.408 --> 00:01:42.950
"Should we run away or stay and talk to them?"

30
00:01:43.211 --> 00:01:43.811
Gliss asked.

31
00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:46.733
"They look pretty friendly," Perda said.

32
00:01:46.753 --> 00:01:50.975
"Besides, I'm guessing we can outrun them if we have to."

33
00:01:52.156 --> 00:01:54.757
Several minutes later the natives reached the visitors.

34
00:01:54.777 --> 00:01:59.560
"Greetings, strangers," one of them said.

35
00:02:00.544 --> 00:02:02.445
His voice was slow but friendly.

36
00:02:03.585 --> 00:02:05.987
"Welcome to Chronos."

37
00:02:06.007 --> 00:02:08.548
"Thank you," Zann said.

38
00:02:08.568 --> 00:02:10.969
"We just arrived through the wormhole."

39
00:02:11.929 --> 00:02:14.170
"Is everything always so slow here?"

40
00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.031
Perda asked.

41
00:02:16.131 --> 00:02:19.553
Long-drawn-out chuckles emerged from several of the Chronians.

42
00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:28.024
"That's the first question every visitor asks," said one Chronian.

43
00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:34.129
"Yes, time moves more slowly here than it does in most other worlds."

44
00:02:35.531 --> 00:02:39.254
"That's right," another Chronian continued.

45
00:02:39.274 --> 00:02:51.664
"For every hour that passes in Chronos, just seconds pass in the vortex or most other worlds."

46
00:02:53.065 --> 00:02:56.328
Zann already felt impatient with the Chronians' slow speech.

47
00:02:57.324 --> 00:02:59.186
"Has anyone else visited lately?"

48
00:02:59.446 --> 00:02:59.886
he asked.

49
00:02:59.906 --> 00:03:01.948
"A woman named Wyssa?"

50
00:03:03.429 --> 00:03:06.432
"Yes," one of the Chronians said.

51
00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:12.737
"Wyssa arrived here earlier.

52
00:03:13.858 --> 00:03:21.185
But she moved on immediately."

53
00:03:22.265 --> 00:03:23.046
Zann frowned.

54
00:03:23.486 --> 00:03:24.888
Their tracking method was working.

55
00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.241
But they couldn't seem to catch up with Wyssa!

56
00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:29.923
"Do you know where she was going next?"

57
00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:30.703
he asked.

58
00:03:30.723 --> 00:03:33.124
"Was it a place called World X?

59
00:03:33.684 --> 00:03:35.065
A newly discovered world?"

60
00:03:35.085 --> 00:03:42.689
"Wyssa wasn't here long enough to tell us about her plans," a Chronian said.

61
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:44.890
Another Chronian spoke up.

62
00:03:48.476 --> 00:03:52.240
"Wait—Wyssa might not have said anything.

63
00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:59.847
But a traveler who passed by a few days ago did mention a new world."

64
00:03:59.867 --> 00:04:02.689
"Really?" Zann spun to face him.

65
00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:06.973
"Was the traveler a tall, skinny guy named Morb?"

66
00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:14.260
"No." A look of confusion passed slowly over the Chronian's face.

67
00:04:15.376 --> 00:04:20.701
"It was a trader who passes through Chronos frequently.

68
00:04:21.902 --> 00:04:25.406
He visits many worlds in his travels."

69
00:04:26.607 --> 00:04:27.448
"What did he say?"

70
00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.109
Zann's heart pounded.

71
00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.232
Could this be the clue that would lead to his parents?

72
00:04:33.093 --> 00:04:35.175
Maybe they wouldn't need to catch Wyssa after all!

73
00:04:35.195 --> 00:04:39.900
"The trader has heard rumors," the Chronian said.

74
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:51.849
"Supposedly there's a world with wormholes that lead not only into the vortex, but directly into other worlds

75
00:04:51.989 --> 00:04:52.870
as well!"

76
00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.853
"But that's not how wormholes work," Perda said.

77
00:04:56.873 --> 00:05:01.717
"You have to travel through the vortex to go from one world to another."

78
00:05:02.718 --> 00:05:03.738
The Chronian shrugged.

79
00:05:04.319 --> 00:05:06.040
"I know.

80
00:05:07.301 --> 00:05:10.484
The trader wasn't sure it was true either.

81
00:05:10.944 --> 00:05:14.745
He hasn't seen this strange world himself."

82
00:05:14.765 --> 00:05:19.507
"If it's real, it could be World X," Zann said.

83
00:05:19.527 --> 00:05:23.948
"It sure sounds like the kind of place that my parents would want to find."

84
00:05:24.869 --> 00:05:25.949
He glanced at his friends.

85
00:05:25.969 --> 00:05:27.009
"We should go!"

86
00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.611
Perda yawned and reached for another pancake.

87
00:05:30.631 --> 00:05:34.692
"Why don't we rest here for a little while first?

88
00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:41.245
You heard what they said—even if we stay here for hours, only a few seconds will pass everywhere

89
00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:47.030
else." Zann wanted to argue, but he could see that his friends were hungry and tired.

90
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.171
"All right," he said.

91
00:05:49.191 --> 00:05:52.174
"But let's make it a short rest, okay?"

92
00:05:53.955 --> 00:05:56.678
The Chronians led them to a gray town nearby.

93
00:05:57.518 --> 00:06:03.103
The local innkeeper offered the visitors food and drink, which was nearly tasteless but filling.

94
00:06:04.268 --> 00:06:06.930
Then she showed Zann and his friends to comfortable beds.

95
00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.292
Zann was sure he'd never be able to sleep.

96
00:06:11.092 --> 00:06:14.394
But he drifted off quickly and fell into another vivid dream.

97
00:06:15.395 --> 00:06:20.598
His parents were running in terror through a forest with dark magic swirling around them.

98
00:06:21.578 --> 00:06:24.840
Like everything else in Chronos, the dream moved slowly.

99
00:06:25.721 --> 00:06:29.603
That gave Zann time to see details he hadn't noticed in his previous dreams.

100
00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:35.579
In the forest there were tiny houses with doors no higher than his mother's knee.

101
00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:41.803
While the forest seemed dark, the sky overhead was a brilliant shade of blue.

102
00:06:42.904 --> 00:06:46.066
Zann finally awoke, blinking in the pale gray light.

103
00:06:46.966 --> 00:06:50.128
Could anything in his dream be a clue to finding his parents?

104
00:06:51.089 --> 00:06:52.910
Lots of worlds had blue skies.

105
00:06:53.751 --> 00:06:56.453
But not many worlds had such tiny houses.

106
00:06:57.473 --> 00:07:01.056
Even Fud from Galvan was too big to fit through those small doors.

107
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.501
Eager to get moving, Zann woke his friends.

108
00:07:05.441 --> 00:07:09.002
It seemed to take forever for the Chronians to guide them back to the wormhole.

109
00:07:09.942 --> 00:07:14.904
Then Zann had to wait for the mutual shackles to appear, and for the wormhole to open.

110
00:07:15.784 --> 00:07:18.585
But finally he and his friends were back in the vortex.

111
00:07:18.605 --> 00:07:22.866
"Wow," Gliss said as wormholes rushed past.

112
00:07:22.886 --> 00:07:27.147
"It feels weird to be living at full speed again."

113
00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:31.296
"Yeah." Darb looked at Zann.

114
00:07:31.436 --> 00:07:32.757
"Hey, the purple mark is glowing!"

115
00:07:32.777 --> 00:07:37.939
"Good." Zann grabbed the next wormhole and pulled his friends through.

116
00:07:38.979 --> 00:07:43.421
The world they landed in was dark, with jagged lightning splitting the sky.

117
00:07:44.441 --> 00:07:46.322
Zann recognized it and gasped.

118
00:07:47.042 --> 00:07:48.943
Apparently Perda recognized it too.

119
00:07:49.843 --> 00:07:50.443
"Oh no!

120
00:07:51.183 --> 00:07:51.684
We're back
